Here is the complete cost and profit breakdown for the XPlay Core Edition (512GB) using your upper-limit expense assumptions:
XPlay Core Edition (512GB) — Cost & Profit Breakdown
Expense / Revenue Item	Amount (INR)	Notes
NVMe SSD (Foxin 512GB PCIe 3.0)	₹7,900	₹7,899 Amazon list price (Micron chipset + SMI controller, 5-Yr warranty)
10Gbps Aluminum Enclosure	₹1,000	Includes USB-C & USB-A cables + thermal pad
Wireless Controller	₹0	Not included in Core Edition
Free Welcome Game Key	₹0	Not included (plays Free-to-Play Steam/Epic & retro titles)
Custom Packing Box + Vinyl Skin	₹500	Your upper-limit packaging budget
Printed Cards & Void Security Seal	₹200	Quick-Start/Warranty card + tamper-evident sticker
Outer Shipping Box + Bubble Wrap	₹300	Protective transit packaging
Insured Pan-India Courier (Shiprocket)	₹300	Doorstep delivery with transit insurance
Razorpay Payment Gateway Fee	₹300	~2.36% transaction fee on ₹12,499
Total All-In Cost	₹10,500	Exact manufacturing + fulfillment cost
Recommended Selling Price	₹12,499 (or ₹12,999)	Keeps entry price ~₹6,000 lower than Pocket Console (₹18,499)
Guaranteed Net Profit Per Unit	₹1,999 (₹2,499 at ₹12,999)	~16% – 19% net margin
Key Pricing Takeaways
Why ₹12,499 Works Best: Even with your conservative upper-limit estimates for packaging and shipping (₹1,300 combined), selling at ₹12,499 locks in a safe ₹1,999 net profit per order.
Real-World Bonus Margin: Since actual box printing, cards, and Shiprocket courier costs for a compact drive-only parcel will realistically land closer to ₹500–₹600 (instead of ₹1,300), your real net profit will likely be ₹2,700+ per unit.
Clear Upgrade Ladder: Having Core at ₹12,499, Pocket Console at ₹18,499, and Pro Edition at ₹27,999 creates a clean ₹6,000–₹9,500 step-up between tiers without any cannibalization.
